<title>USA: Texas Instruments chooses Andersen.</title>
<headline>Texas Instruments chooses Andersen.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andersen Consulting said it will design, build and maintain Texas Instruments Semiconductor Group's open business information systems under a five-year contract is valued at more than $200 million.</p>
<p>Under the agreement effective January 1, Andersen Consulting said it will develop client/server software for use in key Texas Instruments Inc business processes and ultimately integrate and maintain its client/server systems.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Andersen Consulting said, it will hire about 250 TI information systems employees to be part of its new end-to-end offering, Design, Build, Run.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
